<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{ app.request.locale|default('en') }}">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>{% block page_title %}Admin{% endblock %}</title>
    {# Applied before any CSS paints, not after - reading this in a normal
       body-level script would show the light theme for one frame then
       flash to dark. "auto" (the default - no explicit choice saved yet)
       intentionally sets no attribute at all: the plain
       @media(prefers-color-scheme:dark) rule below already covers it, no
       need to duplicate that logic in JS too. #}
    <script>
        (function () {
            var saved = localStorage.getItem('admin-theme');
            if (saved === 'light' || saved === 'dark') {
                document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', saved);
            }
        })();
    </script>
    {% block head_stylesheets %}
    <style>
        :root {
            --admin-bg: #f6f7f9; --admin-surface: #fff; --admin-border: #e3e6ea;
            --admin-text: #1f2429; --admin-muted: #6b7683; --admin-accent: #2563eb;
            --admin-danger: #dc2626; --admin-radius: 8px;
        }
        {# "auto" (no data-theme attribute at all) follows the OS - explicit
           data-theme="dark"/"light" (set above from a saved preference)
           always wins regardless of OS setting. #}
        @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
            :root:not([data-theme="light"]) {
                --admin-bg: #16181d; --admin-surface: #1e2127; --admin-border: #2c3038;
                --admin-text: #e6e8eb; --admin-muted: #8b94a1; --admin-accent: #6ea8fe;
                --admin-danger: #f87171;
            }
        }
        :root[data-theme="dark"] {
            --admin-bg: #16181d; --admin-surface: #1e2127; --admin-border: #2c3038;
            --admin-text: #e6e8eb; --admin-muted: #8b94a1; --admin-accent: #6ea8fe;
            --admin-danger: #f87171;
        }
        .admin-topbar { display: flex; justify-content: flex-end; align-items: center; padding: .6rem .9rem; margin: -1.5rem -2rem 1.25rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--admin-border); }
        .admin-theme-switch { position: relative; }
        .admin-theme-switch > button { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .4rem; padding: .35rem .7rem; border-radius: 6px; border: 1px solid var(--admin-border);
            background: var(--admin-surface); color: inherit; cursor: pointer; font: inherit; font-size: .85rem; }
        .admin-theme-switch > button:hover { border-color: var(--admin-accent); color: var(--admin-accent); }
        .admin-theme-menu { display: none; position: absolute; top: calc(100% + .3rem); right: 0; min-width: 150px; z-index: 20;
            background: var(--admin-surface); border: 1px solid var(--admin-border); border-radius: var(--admin-radius); box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,.15); overflow: hidden; }
        .admin-theme-switch.is-open .admin-theme-menu { display: block; }
        .admin-theme-menu button { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .5rem; width: 100%; padding: .5rem .8rem; border: 0; background: none; text-align: left;
            color: inherit; cursor: pointer; font: inherit; font-size: .85rem; }
        .admin-theme-menu button:hover { background: var(--admin-bg); }
        .admin-theme-menu button.is-active { color: var(--admin-accent); font-weight: 600; }
        .admin-theme-menu button i { width: 1rem; text-align: center; }
        * { box-sizing: border-box; }
        body { margin: 0; font: 15px/1.5 system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; background: var(--admin-bg); color: var(--admin-text); }
        .admin-shell { display: flex; min-height: 100vh; }
        .admin-aside { width: 230px; flex-shrink: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; background: var(--admin-surface); border-right: 1px solid var(--admin-border); padding: 1rem 0; }
        .admin-aside .brand { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .5rem; padding: 0 1.25rem .75rem; font-weight: 700; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--admin-border); }
        .admin-menu { list-style: none; margin: .75rem 0 0; padding: 0; }
        .admin-menu .section { padding: .9rem 1.25rem .3rem; font-size: .78rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .04em; color: var(--admin-muted); }
        .admin-menu a { display: block; padding: .45rem 1.25rem; color: inherit; text-decoration: none; border-left: 3px solid transparent; }
        .admin-menu a:hover { background: var(--admin-bg); }
        .admin-menu .selected > a { border-left-color: var(--admin-accent); color: var(--admin-accent); font-weight: 600; }
        .admin-menu a i { width: 1.1rem; text-align: center; margin-right: .3rem; }
        .admin-menu .sub a { padding-left: 2.75rem; font-size: .92rem; }
        .admin-usermenu { margin-top: auto; padding-top: .75rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--admin-border); }
        .admin-usermenu a i { width: 1.1rem; text-align: center; }
        .admin-analytics { padding: .75rem 1.25rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--admin-border); font-size: .8rem; color: var(--admin-muted); }
        .admin-analytics .analytics-window { font-size: .72rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .04em; margin: .5rem 0 .2rem; }
        .admin-analytics .analytics-window:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
        .admin-analytics .row { margin: .1rem 0; }
        .admin-main { flex: 1; padding: 1.5rem 2rem; min-width: 0; }
        .admin-header { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
        .admin-header h1 { margin: 0; font-size: 1.35rem; }
        .admin-header .global-actions { margin-left: auto; display: flex; gap: .5rem; }
        .card { background: var(--admin-surface); border: 1px solid var(--admin-border); border-radius: var(--admin-radius); }
        .btn { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .4rem; padding: .45rem .9rem; border-radius: 6px; border: 1px solid var(--admin-border);
               background: var(--admin-surface); color: inherit; text-decoration: none; font-size: .9rem; cursor: pointer; }
        .btn:hover { border-color: var(--admin-accent); color: var(--admin-accent); }
        .btn-primary { background: var(--admin-accent); border-color: var(--admin-accent); color: #fff; }
        .btn-primary:hover { color: #fff; filter: brightness(1.08); }
        .text-danger, .btn.text-danger { color: var(--admin-danger); }
        table.datagrid { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; }
        .datagrid th, .datagrid td { text-align: left; padding: .6rem .9rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--admin-border); }
        .datagrid th a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
        .datagrid tr:hover td { background: var(--admin-bg); }
        .datagrid td.actions, .datagrid th.actions { text-align: right; white-space: nowrap; }
        .datagrid .actions a, .datagrid .actions button { margin-left: .35rem; }
        .paginator { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .75rem; padding: .75rem .9rem; color: var(--admin-muted); font-size: .9rem; }
        .paginator .pages { margin-left: auto; display: flex; gap: .25rem; }
        form.admin-form .form-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(12, 1fr); gap: 0 1.25rem; padding: 1.25rem; }
        form.admin-form .form-row { grid-column: span var(--col-span, 12); min-width: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
        form.admin-form label { display: block; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: .3rem; }
        form.admin-form input[type=text], form.admin-form input[type=email], form.admin-form input[type=number],
        form.admin-form input[type=password], form.admin-form select, form.admin-form textarea {
            width: 100%; padding: .5rem .65rem; border: 1px solid var(--admin-border); border-radius: 6px; font: inherit; background: var(--admin-bg);
        }
        form.admin-form .form-errors { color: var(--admin-danger); font-size: .85rem; margin-top: .25rem; }
        @media (max-width: 720px) { form.admin-form .form-row { grid-column: span 12 !important; } }
        {# BooleanField's confirm-modal markup (form_div_layout.html.twig) is
           Bootstrap ".modal fade" markup: it only ever hides/shows via
           Bootstrap's own CSS+JS, neither of which this package loads (no
           Bootstrap anywhere in the admin by design) - so it's permanently
           inert either way, and left unstyled it renders as a big block of
           plain in-flow text. Hiding it isn't a functional regression, just
           containment of dead markup until/unless a real confirm
           interaction is built for it. #}
        form.admin-form .modal.fade { display: none; }
        {# select2/tag widgets otherwise compute their own fixed pixel width
           from the underlying <select> at init time, which can end up
           narrower than - or fail to track - their actual CSS grid column
           once ->setColumns() puts them in something less than the full
           12-span. Forcing 100% keeps them honest to the grid track. #}
        form.admin-form .select2-container { width: 100% !important; }
        .form-footer { display: flex; gap: .5rem; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--admin-border); }
        dl.detail { padding: 1.25rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr; gap: .5rem 1rem; margin: 0; }
        dl.detail dt { font-weight: 600; color: var(--admin-muted); }
        dl.detail dd { margin: 0; }
        .empty-state { padding: 3rem; text-align: center; color: var(--admin-muted); }
        .flashes { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
        .flash { padding: .6rem .9rem; border-radius: 6px; margin-bottom: .4rem; border: 1px solid var(--admin-border); background: var(--admin-surface); }
        .flash-success { border-color: #86efac; background: #f0fdf4; color: #166534; }
        .flash-warning { border-color: #fde68a; background: #fffbeb; color: #92400e; }
        .flash-danger, .flash-error { border-color: #fecaca; background: #fef2f2; color: #991b1b; }
        .search-form { display: inline-flex; gap: .4rem; }
        .search-form input { padding: .45rem .65rem; border: 1px solid var(--admin-border); border-radius: 6px; font: inherit; min-width: 220px; }
        .quick-access { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(180px, 1fr)); gap: .75rem; padding: 1.25rem; }
        .quick-access a { display: block; padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--admin-border); border-radius: var(--admin-radius); text-decoration: none; color: inherit; background: var(--admin-surface); }
        .quick-access a:hover { border-color: var(--admin-accent); color: var(--admin-accent); }
        .filter-bar { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: flex-end; gap: .75rem; padding: .75rem .9rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;
                      background: var(--admin-surface); border: 1px solid var(--admin-border); border-radius: var(--admin-radius); }
        .filter-bar label { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: .2rem; font-size: .82rem; color: var(--admin-muted); }
        .filter-bar input, .filter-bar select { padding: .4rem .55rem; border: 1px solid var(--admin-border); border-radius: 6px; font: inherit; background: var(--admin-bg); }
        .filter-bar .filter-range { display: flex; gap: .3rem; }
        .datagrid th.batch, .datagrid td.batch { width: 2rem; text-align: center; }

        {# ── Field-type templates (crud/field/*.html.twig) ──────────────── #}
        .badge { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .3rem; padding: .15rem .55rem; border-radius: 999px;
                 background: var(--admin-bg); border: 1px solid var(--admin-border); font-size: .8rem; line-height: 1.5; white-space: nowrap; }
        .badge i { font-size: .75rem; }
        .badge-accent { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--admin-accent) 12%, transparent); border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--admin-accent) 35%, transparent); color: var(--admin-accent); }
        .badge-muted { color: var(--admin-muted); }
        .badge-list { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .3rem; }

        .field-switch { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; cursor: pointer; }
        .field-switch input { position: absolute; opacity: 0; width: 1px; height: 1px; }
        .field-switch .track { width: 34px; height: 19px; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--admin-border); position: relative; transition: background .15s ease; flex: 0 0 auto; }
        .field-switch .track::after { content: ''; position: absolute; top: 2px; left: 2px; width: 15px; height: 15px; border-radius: 50%; background: #fff; box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3); transition: transform .15s ease; }
        .field-switch input:checked + .track { background: var(--admin-accent); }
        .field-switch input:checked + .track::after { transform: translateX(15px); }
        .field-switch.is-saving { opacity: .6; pointer-events: none; }

        .field-color { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .4rem; }
        .field-color .swatch { width: 15px; height: 15px; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.15); flex: 0 0 auto; }

        .field-country { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .4rem; }
        .field-country .flag { font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1; }

        .field-media { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .5rem; }
        .field-media img, .field-media .avatar { width: 32px; height: 32px; border-radius: 6px; object-fit: cover; border: 1px solid var(--admin-border); background: var(--admin-bg); }
        .field-media .avatar { border-radius: 50%; }
        .field-media a { color: inherit; }

        .field-mono { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
        .field-money, .field-number { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }

        .field-id { color: var(--admin-muted); font-size: .85rem; }
        .field-id a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
        .field-id a:hover { color: var(--admin-accent); }

        .field-slug code { background: var(--admin-bg); border: 1px solid var(--admin-border); border-radius: 4px; padding: .1rem .4rem; font-size: .85em; }
        .field-slug .lock { color: var(--admin-muted); font-size: .8em; margin-left: .3rem; }

        .field-translatable { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .4rem; }
        .field-translatable .locale-dot { width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%; display: inline-block; }
        .field-translatable .locale-dot.is-complete { background: #22c55e; }
        .field-translatable .locale-dot.is-missing { background: var(--admin-border); }

        .field-association a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px dotted var(--admin-muted); }
        .field-association a:hover { color: var(--admin-accent); border-color: var(--admin-accent); }
        .batch-toolbar { padding: .6rem .9rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--admin-border); }
        .manual-menu-section { margin-top: .5rem; }
        .manual-tree { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; }
        .manual-tree a { display: block; padding: .3rem 1.25rem; color: inherit; text-decoration: none; font-size: .92rem; }
        .manual-tree a:hover { color: var(--admin-accent); }
        .manual-tree li.selected > a { color: var(--admin-accent); font-weight: 600; }
        .manual-content { padding: 1.5rem; }
        .manual-meta { text-align: right; color: var(--admin-muted); font-size: .82rem; margin-bottom: .5rem; }
        .manual-excerpt { color: var(--admin-muted); }
    </style>
    {% endblock %}
    {% block form_assets %}
        {# base-bundle's prebuilt widget bundles (select2, editor, datetime,
           color, dropzone, ...) - published under /bundles/base and resolved
           through its WebpackTagRenderer; the widgets initialise themselves
           from DOM markers rendered by @Base/form/form_div_layout.html.twig #}
        {{ encore_entry_link_tags('form') }}
        {{ encore_entry_script_tags('form') }}
        {# FontAwesome's class rules (.fa-solid/.fas/.far/...) live in the
           'base' entry's CSS, not 'form' - the font FILES were always
           reachable, but nothing mapped fa-* classes to glyphs, so every
           icon referenced by field/action config (IconField, EmailField,
           row action icons, ...) rendered as invisible/blank. CSS only -
           no need for 'base''s JS here. #}
        {{ encore_entry_link_tags('base') }}
        {# One SPA engine for the whole product: transparentJS, vendored here
           as plain UMD scripts (no Encore/webpack involvement - the package
           has no build step of its own). Same library the public site and
           the website-in-website overlay use; in-admin navigation now works
           the same way everything else does: AJAX swap of #page, cached
           pages, fade transitions - instead of a hard reload per click. #}
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('bundles/admin/css/transparent.css') }}">
        <script src="{{ asset('bundles/admin/js/jquery.min.js') }}"></script>
        <script src="{{ asset('bundles/admin/js/transparent.js') }}"></script>
        <script>
            // Transparent.ready() was NEVER being called here - meaning
            // `isReady` stayed false forever, and __main__'s early-return
            // for that case does NOT call e.preventDefault() first. Every
            // click on every admin link was silently falling through to a
            // real, hard browser navigation of this iframe (not the AJAX
            // swap the rest of this layout's comments and markup assume) -
            // confirmed live: a genuine multi-hundred-ms blank-white gap
            // (a real page load, not a styled transition) on every single
            // in-admin navigation. {once:true} matters here exactly like it
            // does on the public site's equivalent call (see
            // assets/app-defer.js): transparent.js re-dispatches a
            // synthetic 'load' event on every SPA nav, so a non-once
            // listener would re-run ready() (and its side effects) on every
            // click inside the admin too.
            window.addEventListener('load', function () {
                if (!window.Transparent) return;
                Transparent.ready({
                    // Confine the SPA swap to /admin/* - a link out to the
                    // public site (e.g. a "view online" link on an
                    // article) should be a plain navigation, not an
                    // attempt to AJAX-swap the whole unrelated page into
                    // this frame.
                    exceptions: [/^(?!\/admin(\/|$)).*/]
                });
            }, { once: true });
        </script>
        <script>
            // crud/field/boolean.html.twig's inline switch: a delegated
            // listener on `document` (not the individual checkboxes)
            // survives every future in-admin AJAX swap without needing to
            // be re-bound - #page's content gets replaced, document itself
            // never does.
            //
            // Listens for 'click' on the LABEL and manages `checked`
            // itself (e.preventDefault() on the native forwarding),
            // rather than listening for 'change' and trusting the browser
            // to forward a label click to its nested checkbox first -
            // one less moving part between "user clicked" and "we know
            // the new value", and avoids depending on exactly how/when
            // that native forwarding fires.
            document.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
                const label = e.target.closest('.field-switch');
                if (!label) return;
                e.preventDefault();

                const input = label.querySelector('input[type=checkbox]');
                const previousChecked = input.checked;
                const url = label.dataset.toggleUrl;
                const property = label.dataset.property;
                const token = label.dataset.token;

                input.checked = !previousChecked;
                label.classList.add('is-saving');
                fetch(url, {
                    method: 'PATCH',
                    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
                    body: JSON.stringify({ property: property, _token: token }),
                }).then(function (response) {
                    if (!response.ok) throw new Error('toggle failed');
                    return response.json();
                }).then(function (data) {
                    input.checked = !!data.value;
                }).catch(function () {
                    input.checked = previousChecked; // revert on any failure
                }).finally(function () {
                    label.classList.remove('is-saving');
                });
            });
        </script>
        <script>
            // Topbar appearance dropdown - same delegated-on-document
            // pattern as the boolean switch above, for the same reason
            // (survives future in-admin AJAX swaps with nothing to
            // rebind). One listener handles both opening/closing the menu
            // and picking a choice from it.
            document.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
                const swtch = document.querySelector('[data-theme-switch]');
                if (!swtch) return;

                const choiceBtn = e.target.closest('[data-theme-choice]');
                if (choiceBtn) {
                    const choice = choiceBtn.dataset.themeChoice;
                    if (choice === 'auto') {
                        localStorage.removeItem('admin-theme');
                        document.documentElement.removeAttribute('data-theme');
                    } else {
                        localStorage.setItem('admin-theme', choice);
                        document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', choice);
                    }
                    swtch.classList.remove('is-open');
                    swtch.querySelector('button[aria-haspopup]').setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
                    return;
                }

                const toggleBtn = e.target.closest('[data-theme-switch] > button');
                if (toggleBtn) {
                    const isOpen = swtch.classList.toggle('is-open');
                    toggleBtn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', isOpen ? 'true' : 'false');
                    return;
                }

                // click anywhere else closes it
                swtch.classList.remove('is-open');
                swtch.querySelector('button[aria-haspopup]').setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
            });
            // reflect the saved/current choice with an "active" mark and
            // keep it in sync if the OS theme changes while "system" is
            // selected (no saved override) - re-runs the same tiny check
            // rather than needing a page reload to notice.
            (function () {
                function markActive() {
                    var saved = localStorage.getItem('admin-theme') || 'auto';
                    document.querySelectorAll('[data-theme-choice]').forEach(function (btn) {
                        btn.classList.toggle('is-active', btn.dataset.themeChoice === saved);
                    });
                }
                markActive();
                document.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
                    if (e.target.closest('[data-theme-choice]')) markActive();
                });
            })();
        </script>
    {% endblock %}
</head>
<body>
{# id="page": transparentJS only engages its SPA click/swap handling when
   the current document contains this element (same convention the public
   site's base.html.twig uses) - everything inside it is what gets swapped
   and cached on navigation. #}
<div id="page" class="admin-shell">
    <aside class="admin-aside">
        <div class="brand">
            {% block brand %}<span>{% block brand_title %}Administration{% endblock %}</span>{% endblock %}
        </div>
        {% block main_menu %}
            {% if admin_context is defined and admin_context.mainMenu is not empty %}
            <ul class="admin-menu">
                {% for item in admin_context.mainMenu %}
                    {% if item.section %}
                        <li class="section">{{ item.label|trans({}, 'admin') }}</li>
                    {% else %}
                        <li class="{{ item.selected ? 'selected' }}">
                            <a href="{{ item.linkUrl ?? '#' }}"{% if item.linkTarget %} target="{{ item.linkTarget }}"{% endif %}>{% if item.icon %}<i class="{{ item.icon }}"></i> {% endif %}{{ item.label|trans({}, 'admin') }}</a>
                        </li>
                        {% for subItem in item.subItems %}
                            <li class="{{ subItem.selected ? 'selected' }} sub"><a href="{{ subItem.linkUrl ?? '#' }}">{% if subItem.icon %}<i class="{{ subItem.icon }}"></i> {% endif %}{{ subItem.label|trans({}, 'admin') }}</a></li>
                        {% endfor %}
                    {% endif %}
                {% endfor %}
            </ul>
            {% endif %}
        {% endblock %}
        {% block user_menu %}
            {% if admin_context is defined and admin_context.userMenu is not empty %}
            <ul class="admin-menu admin-usermenu">
                {% for item in admin_context.userMenu %}
                    <li><a href="{{ item.linkUrl ?? '#' }}">{% if item.icon %}<i class="{{ item.icon }}"></i> {% endif %}{{ item.label|trans({}, 'admin') }}</a></li>
                {% endfor %}
            </ul>
            {% endif %}
        {% endblock %}
        {# Base\Service\Analytics's page-view/visitor/user counters, via the
           Twig functions base-bundle's AnalyticsTwigExtension exposes - a
           single summary() call gets every window in one round trip. #}
        {% block analytics_widget %}
            {% set stats = analytics_summary() %}
            <div class="admin-analytics">
                <div class="analytics-window">{{ 'analytics.today'|trans({}, 'admin') }}</div>
                <div class="row">{{ 'analytics.page_views'|trans({'%count%': stats.today.pageViews}, 'admin') }}</div>
                <div class="row">{{ 'analytics.unique_visitors'|trans({'%count%': stats.today.uniqueVisitors}, 'admin') }}</div>
                {% if stats.today.uniqueUsers > 0 %}
                <div class="row">{{ 'analytics.unique_users'|trans({'%count%': stats.today.uniqueUsers}, 'admin') }}</div>
                {% endif %}
                <div class="analytics-window">{{ 'analytics.last_7_days'|trans({}, 'admin') }}</div>
                <div class="row">{{ 'analytics.page_views'|trans({'%count%': stats['7d'].pageViews}, 'admin') }}</div>
                <div class="row">{{ 'analytics.unique_visitors'|trans({'%count%': stats['7d'].uniqueVisitors}, 'admin') }}</div>
                {% if stats['7d'].uniqueUsers > 0 %}
                <div class="row">{{ 'analytics.unique_users'|trans({'%count%': stats['7d'].uniqueUsers}, 'admin') }}</div>
                {% endif %}
            </div>
        {% endblock %}
    </aside>
    <main class="admin-main">
        {% block topbar %}
            <div class="admin-topbar">
                <div class="admin-theme-switch" data-theme-switch>
                    <button type="button" aria-haspopup="true" aria-expanded="false">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-half-stroke"></i> {{ 'topbar.appearance'|trans({}, 'admin') }}
                    </button>
                    <div class="admin-theme-menu" role="menu">
                        <button type="button" data-theme-choice="light"><i class="fa-solid fa-sun"></i> {{ 'topbar.theme_light'|trans({}, 'admin') }}</button>
                        <button type="button" data-theme-choice="dark"><i class="fa-solid fa-moon"></i> {{ 'topbar.theme_dark'|trans({}, 'admin') }}</button>
                        <button type="button" data-theme-choice="auto"><i class="fa-solid fa-desktop"></i> {{ 'topbar.theme_auto'|trans({}, 'admin') }}</button>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        {% endblock %}
        {% block flashes %}
            {% set flashes = app.flashes %}
            {% if flashes is not empty %}
            <div class="flashes">
                {% for type, messages in flashes %}
                    {% for message in messages %}
                        <div class="flash flash-{{ type }}">{{ message|trans }}</div>
                    {% endfor %}
                {% endfor %}
            </div>
            {% endif %}
        {% endblock %}
        {% block content_header %}{% endblock %}
        {% block content %}{% endblock %}
    </main>
</div>
{% block body_javascript %}{% endblock %}
{# NOT calling parent.Transparent.notifyNestReady() here (tried it,
   reverted - see git history / transparent.js's mount()). A plain
   inline <script> this close to </body> still runs during HTML
   PARSING, roughly DOMContentLoaded timing, well before images/
   stylesheets/deferred scripts have actually finished loading and
   applied. Measured directly against the real admin dashboard: firing
   it unconditionally here revealed the overlay while this document's
   readyState was still "interactive", 668ms before it reached
   "complete" - the exact "page goes white, nested site hasn't finished
   loading" bug. Gating it on this document's OWN 'load' event instead
   just re-races the parent's identical 'load'-driven reveal with no
   guaranteed ordering between the two, for no proven benefit - this
   app's actual asset loading (form-defer included, all real <script>
   tags) is already fully covered by the parent's load+settle fallback
   in Transparent.nest's mount(). Reconsider notifyNestReady() only if a
   future page here has real async work that genuinely continues after
   its own 'load' event. #}
</html>
